  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decent work effectively mainstreamed in the agenda and programmes of regional and sub regional partner institutions, including the AU UN, and the AfDB</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Region will pursue a strategy of deepening and diversifying its partnerships with the objective of integrating the decent work agenda into the agendas and programmes of regional and sub-regional institutions. Furthermore, we will strive to ensure greater alignment between the regional development cooperation portfolio and the programme and budget outcomes. We will also continue to promote the Global Coalition for Social Justice, particularly given the challenging context in Africa. The outcomes include the following: ILO constituents in Africa have been equipped with the knowledge and skills to engage effectively in the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework and DWCP processes; and the Minimum Wage Report for Africa has been validated by the AUC STC.</narrative>
  </description>
